(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// list's methods (Objects/listobject.c)."] [5 1 "// lessThan is a < b as a Go bool (sort's comparison)."] [14 1 "// SortObjects sorts items in place, stably, by keys (nil: the items themselves), reversed when"] [15 1 "// reverse (a reversed sort keeps equal items in their order, as list.sort does). PY5b: a merge sort"] [16 1 "// with binary insertion runs, not Timsort: the same result, not the same sequence of comparisons."] [98 1 "// listCut removes l's items [i:j). A cut before the end makes a new array, the old one left as it was. A cut that empties"] [99 1 "// the list leaves its array for an empty slice of none (not nil: SortList's mark of a list modified while it sorts). Any"] [100 1 "// other cut to the end keeps the array, whose slots past the new length Go's collector still scans: the cut items"] [101 1 "// outlived their last reference and gc.collect() (py-final-1126: as_completed's and Executor.map's yielded futures,"] [102 1 "// `yield fs.pop()`). They are not cleared here: a Go loop over the items (index, count, a comparison) may be running under"] [103 1 "// a Python callback that cut the list, and must see the values it took; the array is noted (listStale) and its slots past"] [104 1 "// the list's length are cleared at the next collection (listScrub)."] [119 1 "// listStaleEntry is a list and its items before a cut to the end (the array it keeps); listStale the latest cuts, a ring"] [120 1 "// (under the GIL)."] [131 1 "// listScrub clears the slots past each noted list's length that its array still holds, and forgets the notes (a"] [132 1 "// collection's start: gc.collect(), the moment at del)."] [145 1 "// SortList is list.sort(key=key, reverse=reverse): the keys computed first, the list empty while it"] [146 1 "// sorts (a mutation during the sort a ValueError)."] [187 47 "// queue 304: list_extend_iter's PyObject_LengthHint"] [246 3 "// the length read again after each comparison, which may change the list (list_remove's Py_SIZE)"] [253 27 "// list_ass_slice clamps: nothing to remove when the list shrank under it"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[36 19] [36 27] [57 31] [60 31] [78 7] [78 16] [81 7] [81 15] [87 27] [135 12] [135 19] [137 24] [176 48] [184 48] [187 32] [199 43] [223 40] [233 54] [242 48] [247 13] [247 31] [262 42] [268 47] [275 47] [282 46] [288 49] [292 26] [292 33]]} (go/file "list.go" :imports [])

